From 5aea989d2d3ca67625d629d0f1dc19f10beb7df9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:09:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 54/88] xhttp: fixes from the review

Configuration: a range as wide as int32 no longer panics (sing-box check for
the XMUX pool sizes, the process for the rest); header names and values, keys
and the session ID alphabet are checked; ECH with its configuration from DNS is
refused over HTTP/3 instead of being dropped; REALITY and uTLS are seen
through the kernel TLS wrapper.

HTTP/3: a QUIC connection whose request failed is closed (http3.Transport
forgot it open); the shared dial no longer dies with the session that started
it; disable_sni is kept.

A download detour that leads back to its own outbound is refused instead of
dialling itself without end; a domain download server resolves when the
outbound's server is an address.

Pool: max_concurrency counts sessions once, as Xray; closing the transport
reaches connections retired while in use; one idle timer per connection;
connections are closed outside the pool lock; the backoff error does not
carry HTTP error types; an upload keeps its connection when the pool backs
off.

An error status fails the session before its body is read; an IPv6 host goes
in brackets; the upload timeout allows for the data; browser versions are
drawn in Xray's order; HTTP/1.1 uploads carry no Accept-Encoding.
